    "faq": [
        {
            "question": "What are the key differences between AG Grid and Handsontable?",
            "answer": "Both are JavaScript data grids with their own UI. Handsontable has a spreadsheet-like interface and formulas through HyperFormula; its documentation does not list pivoting, built-in charts or row grouping by column. AG Grid Community is free for commercial use under the MIT licence, and AG Grid Enterprise adds row grouping, pivoting and integrated charts."
        },
        {
            "question": "Is Handsontable free to use?",
            "answer": "Handsontable has a free licence for non-commercial purposes such as research, private study and evaluation. Production use connected with commercial activity needs a commercial licence. HyperFormula, the formula engine, is free under GPLv3 for non-commercial or open-source projects and otherwise needs its own commercial licence."
        },
        {
            "question": "How is Handsontable priced?",
            "answer": "Handsontable does not publish prices. Its commercial licence is priced by the number of end users of the applications you build, and is sold through its sales team as a subscription or perpetual licence."
        },
        {
            "question": "Does Handsontable support pivot tables?",
            "answer": "Handsontable's documentation does not list a pivot table feature. AG Grid includes [pivoting](./pivoting/) in AG Grid Enterprise."
        },
        {
            "question": "Can I use AG Grid for free?",
            "answer": "Yes. AG Grid Community is free and open source under the MIT licence, including for commercial use. AG Grid Enterprise is a paid licence that adds features such as row grouping, pivoting, Excel export and the Server-Side Row Model. See [Community vs Enterprise](./community-vs-enterprise/)."
        },
        {
            "question": "How much does an AG Grid licence cost?",
            "answer": "AG Grid Community is free. AG Grid Enterprise, and the Enterprise Bundle with AG Charts Enterprise, are perpetual licences priced per developer, with one year of updates and support. [Configure your licence](/license-pricing/) to see your price."
        }
    ],
